rnally consistent at this head because of the stale \"live and fresh\" statement, so approval is blocked.\n\nSecurity: retired-basis refusal and its explicit recorded override remain intact; the guarded reassignment still checks both claim race windows (promise and direct completion) at the authoritative fold/admission boundary. The stale/staleness body words remain non-authoritative caller-visible metadata, while the fold computes actual staleness from signed provenance; the signing-to-sequencing note gap is disclosed and does not grant authority. I found no unresolved security defect.\n\nSimplification: the single judgeDeadBases split and reuse of reviewguard.StalenessNote are appropriately bounded. No further code abstraction is warranted. The simplest repair is to remove the three obsolete freshness claims and keep one consistent contract across architecture, conceptual guidance, and MCP self-description.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0b963b98df78b091fe098bef4e03242b53c291ef","head":"a398050ae0802ca6793210d1e53d466c317c9eec","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:711e23cfc8469d6a2f400d3a540579f996e1c23c\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:bc53f3f0e1974fca314b2b5c9202ec1df94affb9","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}